  "issue_number": 3964,
  "issue_title": "Homepage KPI panels show \"\u2014\" placeholders forever on both slow load and genuine failure, with no skeleton or error feedback",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\nIn `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx`, `HeroKpis` (lines 322-414), `TrackedGrid` (lines 550-617), and `LivePerformance` (lines 619-668) all use plain `useQuery` (not `useSuspenseQuery`) with no `Suspense` wrapper and no `QueryErrorBoundary` around them. On slow load, they render the pre-fetch fallback (\"\u2014\"/undefined values) with no skeleton shimmer; on a genuine fetch failure, they render the exact same \"\u2014\" dashes. There is no way for a user to tell \"still loading,\" \"failed to load,\" and \"value is legitimately unknown\" apart \u2014 all three states look identical. This sits directly above sibling homepage sections that do handle this correctly.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAll three homepage sections must visually distinguish loading, error, and legitimately-empty/unknown states from each other.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- **File to change**: `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx` \u2014 `HeroKpis`, `TrackedGrid`, `LivePerformance`.\n- **What \"done\" looks like concretely**: add a loading skeleton (matching whatever pattern the app's other correctly-handled sections use) for the pending state, and a visually distinct error indicator (not necessarily a full `ErrorState` card if these are compact KPI tiles \u2014 even a small inline error glyph/tooltip per tile is enough) for the failure state, so all three states are distinguishable from each other and from \"\u2014\" meaning \"genuinely no data.\"\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `index.tsx` appears in the diff, covering all three named sections\n- [ ] Loading, error, and legitimately-empty states are now visually distinct from each other for all three sections\n- [ ] A successful load with real data renders exactly as it does today\n- [ ] Includes a before/after screenshot table showing all three states (loading/error/empty) for at least one of the three sections, both themes, per the repo's UI-PR requirement\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Don't change the homepage's KPI data sources or add new metrics.\n- Don't rework sibling homepage sections that already handle this correctly.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: M \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T09:43:09.000Z",
